== Relationship with other airports ==

{{main|Sant Cristòfor Els Aiguamolls Airport}}

[[Sant Cristòfor Els Aiguamolls Airport]], located in the neighbouring [[Els Aiguamolls]] comarca just north of the city boundary, serves as a complementary facility rather than a relief airport. Els Aiguamolls handles domestic and short-haul regional routes, and is used primarily by residents of the northern ciutats — particularly [[Costa Nord (ciutat)|Costa Nord]] — seeking connections to [[Sant Bart]] and [[Nurra]] without transiting the busier Sant Cristòfor International. [[Balboa Airlines]] operates services from Els Aiguamolls, and the airport is connected to the city by commuter rail. The two airports are not formally coordinated but serve distinct markets: Sant Cristòfor International for long-haul and high-density domestic operations, and Els Aiguamolls for domestic point-to-point and regional services.

